BCRA do still run expedition insurance:- 

It is generally pretty good (having paid up for all the accidents CUCC have
had on expo in the last 6 years: one car crash, one broken leg, one broken
pelvis, one perforated eardrum). You only get 80% for gear costs that are
anything to do with cars (crashes, thefts). There were restrictions about
going to the US & Canada, but I think cover is now available there for a
small extra premium.

Not sure if it is availbale to non UK nationals, although our Irishman was
insured last year so it must be possible. It is cheaper if you are a BCRA
member (about 10%). You also get bulk discount (5%) for buying more than #500
of insurance in one go, so do the expo as a job lot.

